+<h2 id="server">Edge servers of the account: GET and PUT /cdn64o/servers</h2>
+<p>Your account class decides how many edge servers your account uses (<a href="{{u "cdn64"}}#server-je-konto">servers per account</a>). <code>GET</code> shows the assignment; with <code>PUT</code>, Business (1 or 2) and Company (1 to all) choose the number.</p>
+<pre><code>curl -X PUT "https://ipv64.net/api/v2/cdn64o/servers" -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"count": 2}'</code></pre>
+<pre><code>{
+  "data": {
+    "count": 2, "max": 4, "all": true, "total": 4, "selectable": true,
+    "assigned": ["…", "…"],
+    "active": ["…", "…"],
+    "edges": [ … ]
+  }
+}</code></pre>
+<div class="table-responsive"><table class="table table-sm">
+	<thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
+	<tbody>
+		<tr><td><code>count</code></td><td>number of servers of the account; in a <code>PUT</code> the number you want, for Company <code>0</code> = all (including future servers)</td></tr>
+		<tr><td><code>max</code>, <code>total</code></td><td>highest number you can choose and number of edge servers overall</td></tr>
+		<tr><td><code>all</code></td><td><code>true</code>: the class may use all servers (Company)</td></tr>
+		<tr><td><code>selectable</code></td><td><code>true</code>: the number can be chosen (Business, Company)</td></tr>
+		<tr><td><code>assigned</code></td><td>the assigned servers (names)</td></tr>
+		<tr><td><code>active</code></td><td>the servers currently in the DNS of your names – if an assigned one fails, its stand-in is listed here</td></tr>
+		<tr><td><code>edges</code></td><td>the servers Node64 opens tunnels to (like <code>edges</code> in the <a href="#uebersicht">overview</a>)</td></tr>
+	</tbody>
+</table></div>
+<p>Errors: class without a choice <code>403</code> (<code>plan_not_allowed</code>), number out of range <code>422</code> (<code>out_of_range</code>). After a <code>PUT</code>, IPv64.net updates the DNS of all names of the account; each changed name gets the event <code>servers_changed</code>.</p>
+
